  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA, pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while config_010 (image, resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8%, a ~28-point gap. This leaves major uncertainty about whether the image modality is fundamentally uninformative or simply poorly encoded by resnet50. Question: config_013 swaps only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (a larger, ViT-based architecture), keeping everything else identical to config_010. This isolates the effect of image representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in multimodal fusion (configs 016-051) or multiprofile/aggregation strategies, we need to know whether the image modality can be made competitive. If imagenet_vit_l substantially closes the gap, multimodal experiments become high-value and we should prioritize them. If it does not, we can deprioritize image and multimodal paths and focus budget on RNA encoder improvements (scvi_n200, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This single-variable change maximally reduces strategic uncertainty with one experiment."
}

